{
  "title": "pairbench",
  "summary": "pairbench says whether one side is really faster than another on a workload, on one machine, or whether the difference is noise.",
  "details": "A side is a container image, a command, a Python environment, a server image or a set of result files. pairbench runs every side in paired, alternating rounds together with an identical twin of each side, measures the noise floor from the twins in the same rounds, tests each case with an exact sign test, corrects for testing several cases at once, and gives a verdict per case: FASTER, SLOWER, TIE, UNRESOLVED or NO VERDICT, with the reason. Programs read `comparisons[].outcome` and `comparisons[].reason` in `results.json` and quote numbers from its `figures`; `pairbench fill` puts those figures into documents.",
